🔴 1. Missing Input Validation (HIGH PRIORITY)
Problem: Your functions don't validate inputs, which can cause crashes.

Example from index.html:1080-1083:

const calculateLineCFT = (l, w, t, qty) => {
    const feet = getPurchasedFeet(l);
    return ((feet * w * t) / 144) * qty;
};

What happens if user enters:

Negative numbers? → Wrong results
Zero? → Returns 0 (okay)
Non-numbers? → NaN breaks everything
Empty string? → NaN
Fix: Add validation:

const calculateLineCFT = (l, w, t, qty) => {
    // Validate inputs
    if (l <= 0 || w <= 0 || t <= 0 || qty <= 0) return 0;
    if (isNaN(l) || isNaN(w) || isNaN(t) || isNaN(qty)) return 0;
    
    const feet = getPurchasedFeet(l);
    return ((feet * w * t) / 144) * qty;
};

🔴 2. No Error Handling (HIGH PRIORITY)
The 3D visualization (Three.js) could crash and break the entire app. Add error boundaries:

// Wrap your main app
class ErrorBoundary extends React.Component {
    state = { hasError: false };
    
    static getDerivedStateFromError(error) {
        return { hasError: true };
    }
    
    componentDidCatch(error, info) {
        console.error('App crashed:', error, info);
    }
    
    render() {
        if (this.state.hasError) {
            return <div>Something went wrong. Please refresh.</div>;
        }
        return this.props.children;
    }
}

